  "raw_text": "146\n\nSilp luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto examine by oneself, to meditate\n \n/ examinar\nse a\n \nsí mismo, meditar\n\nTihu luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto deeply examine, to consider deeply, to\n \nanalyze deeply\n, to meditate\n \n/ examinar\n\nprofundamente, considerar profundamente, analizar profundamente, meditar\n\nTihu luki kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndeep thought, deep thinking, meditation\n \n/ pensamiento profundo,\nmeditación\n\nLuki paskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make in your thinking (mind), to create in your thinking (mind)\n \n/ hacer en tu pensamiento\n(mente), crear en tu pensamiento (mente)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-05/20\n):\n \nBaibil sturka aisi kaikma taim, trai muns diara sut takan ba luki paskaia\n \n–\n \nWhen you read a Bible\naccount, try to create all that happened in your thinking\n \n/ Cuando leas un relato bíblico, intenta crear todo lo que sucedió\nen tu pensamiento)\n\nLuki tniwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto trust, to rely, to depend on\n \n/ confiar, contar con, depender de\n\n(Note/Nota: It is more common to use\n \nKasak lukaia\n \nto say:\n \nto believe, to have faith, to have confidence\n \n/ Es más común\nusar\n \nKasak lukaia\n \npara decir “creer, tener fe, tener confianza, confiar”\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20\n):\n \nYawan silp wan karnika ra tniwi lukbiara\n \n–\n \nWe are not to trust in our own strength\n \n/ No debemos\nconfiar en nuestro propia fuerza)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nYawan silp wan lukanka ra tniwi lukbiara\n \n–\n \nWe are not to trust in our own thinking\n \n/ No debemos confiar en\nnuestro propio pensamiento)\n\nLukpara\n \n(v-proh)\n \n–\n \ndo not think\n \n/ no pienses\n\nLukra\n \n(n-concept form / s-forma concepto)\n \n–\n \nthought, thoughts, thinking, idea\n \n/ pensamiento, pensamientos,\nidea\n\nKupia lukra\n \n–\n \nthought, thoughts, thinking, thoughts of the heart, caring thought(s), idea\n \n/ pensamiento,\npensamientos, pensamientos del corazón, pensamiento(s) considerado(s), idea\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfy148\n):\n \nBaibil t\nâ\nnka kasak ba upla kupia lukra ba chens munisa\n \n–\n \nAccurate Bible knowledge changes\n\npeople’s thinking\n \n/ El conocimiento exacto de la Biblia cambia el pensamiento de las\n \npersonas\n)\n\nKupia lukra kuninkira\n \n(\ndb\n-\nJirimaya 17:9\n)\n \n–\n \ndeceivous thoughts, treacherous thoughts\n \n/\n\npensamientos engañosos, pensamientos traicioneros\n\nMistik lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think in an erroneous way, to think in an incorrect way, to have a\n \nmisconception\n \n/ pensar de\n\nmanera errónea, pensar de forma incorrecta, tener una idea errónea\n\nNahara luks, ...\n \n–\n \nthink on this here, ...\n \n/ piensa en esto aquí, ...\n\nNamhpa namhpa lukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nNamhpa lukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto go back and forth in thinking, to doubt, to hesitate\n \n/ ir y\nvenir pensando, dudar, vacilar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n03/20\n):\n \nD\nî\na muni kum kum ba kristian trangsar nani ra yamni munaia namhpa namhpa lukisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhy do\n\nsome hesitate to do good (show hospitality) to\n \nChristians who are strangers?\n \n/ ¿Por qué algunos dudan en hacer el bien\n\n(mostrar hospitalidad) a los cristianos que son extraños?\n)\n\nNamhpa namhpa lukanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nNamhpa lukanka\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndoubt, hesitation, uncertainty\n \n/ duda,\nvacilación, incertidumbre\n\nRait lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto believe to be true\n \n/ creer que es verdad\n\nSibrin lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto feel fear, to feel afraid\n \n/ sentir miedo\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\ndb-Param Marikan 14:7\n):\n \nMan nani bui Gâd ra sibrin luks\n \n–\n \n(You) feel fear of God\n \n/ (Ustedes) sientan temor de Dios)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-11/19\n):\n \nSins Lâka 29:25 aisi ba tânka ra, ¿dîa muni yawan upla ra sibrin lukaia apia sa ki?\n \n–\n \nAccording to\nProverbs 29:25, why must we not feel afraid of people?\n \n/ Según Proverbios 29:25, ¿por qué no debemos tener miedo de\nlas personas?)\n\nSwira lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be ashamed, to be embarrassed\n \n/ estar avergonzado\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nG\nâ\nd Kingka l\nâ\nka dukiara wan swira lukras\n \n–\n \nWe\n \nare not ashamed of God’s Kingdom\n \n/ No nos avergonzamos del\nReino de Dios)\n\nTingki lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think in an appreciative way, to be thankful\n \n/ pensar de manera apreciativa, estar\nagradecido\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/19\n):\n \nDîa dukiara yawan tingki lukisa?\n \n–\n \nFor what are we thankful?\n \n/ ¿De qué estamos agradecidos?)\n\nTnata\n \n(a/t:\n \nNata, Pnata\n)\n \nlukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto imitate, to mock\n \n/ imitar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb\n-\n01/21\n):\n \nNasariu nani ra yawan nahki tnata lukaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nHow can we imitate the Nazirites?\n \n/ Cómo\n\npodemos imitar a los nazareos?)\n\nTrabil taki lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think about trouble happening, to think about problems happening, to worry, to be\nconcerned with, to be anxious\n \n/ pensar en los problemas que suceden, preocuparse, estar ansioso",
